    <section id="not-automatic" class="w-full border-y border-border bg-blue-50/60 py-16 lg:py-24"><div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><div class="mx-auto mb-12 max-w-3xl text-center"><p class="mb-3 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-blue-600 uppercase">Accuracy correction</p><h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl">Programs That Do Not Always Qualify by Themselves</h2><p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-foreground/75">These programs may help in other local, school, provider, or special survivor contexts, but they should not be shown as regular general Lifeline qualifiers without official confirmation.</p></div><div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">{notAlwaysQualify.map((card) => <div class="rounded-2xl border border-blue-100 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">{card.title}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-foreground/75">{card.body}</p></div>)}</div><div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-blue-100 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Special Survivor Benefit Note</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-foreground/75">Survivors of domestic violence, human trafficking, or related crimes may have special temporary Lifeline support rules and extended criteria. Do not mix survivor-only criteria with general Lifeline eligibility. Use official Lifeline survivor guidance and privacy-safe steps.</p></div></div></section>

