    <section id="documents" class="w-full border-y border-border bg-muted/30 py-16 lg:py-24"><div class="mx-auto grid w-full max-w-7xl grid-cols-1 gap-10 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:px-8"><div class="lg:col-span-5"><p class="mb-3 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-blue-600 uppercase">Application proof</p><h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl">Free Tablet Documents Needed</h2><p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-foreground/75">Documents can vary by National Verifier, state system, provider process, Tribal rules, and household situation.</p></div><div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:col-span-7">{documentItems.map((item) => <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-white p-5 shadow-sm"><p class="font-bold text-foreground">{item}</p></div>)}</div></div></section>

    <section id="household-rule" class="w-full bg-white py-16 lg:py-24"><div class="mx-auto grid w-full max-w-7xl grid-cols-1 gap-8 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:px-8"><div class="lg:col-span-6"><p class="mb-3 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-blue-600 uppercase">Household limits</p><h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl">One Benefit Per Household and Household Worksheet</h2><p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-foreground/75">Lifeline generally allows one benefit per household, not one per person. A household means people living together and sharing income and expenses. Roommates, shelters, nursing homes, or separate economic households may need a Household Worksheet. Do not assume every family member can receive a tablet.</p></div><div class="lg:col-span-6"><p class="mb-3 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-blue-600 uppercase">Keep benefit active</p><h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl">Use It or Lose It / Recertification</h2><p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-foreground/75">Users may need to use Lifeline service at least once every 30 days if service is free to them, and they may need annual recertification. If they move or no longer qualify, they should update the provider or official process.</p></div></div></section>

